{{author's notes:

and here's motherfucking "Give Me Somewhere to Stand," the second piece of the "Liar's Heraldry Triptych"

this is such a stupid story

i get it, i should be kind to my past selves, blah blah blah, but seriously--this story is bad

it's bad because it's pretentious and juvenile, yes--all the stories from this period of my life are just like this, it is what it is--but also, the whole fucking point was for me to showcase the darkest, most wretched pieces of my heart, but I was never willing to make myself vulnerable enough to put anything genuinely awful on display, so everyone just whines about power and masks and perception in a really oblique and shoegazing kind of way. nobody's actually a terrible person, they're all just idiot assholes

way to go, hotshot. "Give Me Somewhere to Fucking Stand," the idiot asshole manifesto

ironically, this is the entry in the trilogy that i would most like to return to and transform into its best self. i think that the metaphor through which the concept speaks carries really potent and evocative potential. and I think I could really nail the imagery}}

